<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm after two-day holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm after two-day holiday.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices gained by 100-150 rupees per tonne on Wednesday, reopening after a two-day holiday break, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was firm on limited supply. Soyoil solvent was up by 200 rupees per tonne today. Soyoil refined was steady but undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Dealers said soymeal prices were strong on better export demand. Soymeal yellow was $271-272 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $127-128 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,325 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,300 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
